        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-28T09:09:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the patchset 1, apex_manifest.pb file in every vendor apex was labelled as vendor-accessible vendor_configs_file. But this would be less safe from security perspective. In the patchset 2, I\u0027d like to leave that decision to module owners. In most cases, the default would be okay. (By default, apex_manifest.pb is labelled as system_file and vendor processes don\u0027t have access to read it)\n\nThe reason behind making vendor-accessible apex_manifest.pb is to support reading apex_manifest from the apex directly. This doesn\u0027t mean that vendor processes need to know the internals of the file. Reading the manifest should be hidden by a proper API, but the file still needs to be accessible by SE-linux policy.",
      "parentUuid": "bc8763df_b7ee065d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 14
      },
      "revId": "af73095979facd1e2b5a5bb4e4c8e485f1d2f204",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0729291e_1929f03f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-02T02:46:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok. We had a chat and I understand the need.\n\nWe still haven\u0027t reached out to a consensus about whether introducing a new property is preferred to automatically changing the file context to vendor_file for vendor-installed APEXes, or not. But the decision is not critical and I actually am fine with either way.",
      "parentUuid": "a5621cbd_b8369f27",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 14
      },
      "revId": "af73095979facd1e2b5a5bb4e4c8e485f1d2f204",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "935b779a_5218e467",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 12,
      "author": {
        "id": 1514900
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-02T09:04:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think a property is fine. It integrates easier in Bazel as well, since we don\u0027t need to know, at bazel apex rule analysis time, where it\u0027s going to be installed. It only needs to read an attribute/property.\n\nMy only concern is the name of the property. \"use_file_contexts_as_is\" doesn\u0027t really mean much - how about `hardcode_manifest_entry_in_file_contexts`?",
      "parentUuid": "0729291e_1929f03f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 12,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 14
      },
      "revId": "af73095979facd1e2b5a5bb4e4c8e485f1d2f204",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
